After attempting to bring this, I didn't take into account that this would actually cause the aforementioned inspection error ("pre-existing null check in `Dispose()` triggering a "never null" inspection"):

![](https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/188630652340404224/966081850571366410/unknown.png)

Can still push with an inspection disable comment and a TODO:
```csharp
         protected override void Dispose(bool isDisposing)
         {
             base.Dispose(isDisposing);
 
             // ReSharper disable once ConditionIsAlwaysTrueOrFalseAccordingToNullableAPIContract
             // todo: we probably want to handle this in a better way somehow without disabling inspection.
             if (drawableObject != null)
                 drawableObject.ApplyCustomUpdateState -= updateStateTransforms;
         }
```
but not 100% sure if we just want to leave it like that.
